  "model": "gpt-6-luna",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_luna_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B006",
        "laureates": [
          "Charles L. Bennett",
          "David N. Spergel",
          "Lyman A. Page"
        ],
        "citation": "For precision mapping of cosmic microwave background anisotropies that established a quantitative picture of the universe."
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B004",
    "B020"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged: WMAP remains my preference because it made the cosmic microwave background a precision probe of the universe's contents, age, and evolution. Its conclusions gained support from later observations and other cosmological evidence, making this a mature achievement grounded in nature. The citation should recognize WMAP's precision mapping, not claim the first detection of anisotropies or the whole development of precision cosmology.",
    "case_against": "The central unresolved issue is whether Bennett, Spergel, and Page fairly represent decisive contributions within a large mission team and the wider CMB effort. WMAP also built on COBE and was followed by further measurements, so the boundary of the award must be historically defensible. These questions limit confidence in the attribution, even though they have not changed my preferred configuration.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig argues that conformal field theory is itself a physical discovery because it makes critical systems tractable and explains their properties, rather than serving only as a mathematical technique.",
        "response": "That is a persuasive account of B004's physical content, and I agree that theoretical work should not be discounted simply because it lacks a new experimental realization. The framework's long influence strengthens its case. I still prefer WMAP because its central advance is a direct measurement of the universe, whose interpretation can be checked against independent evidence."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "olsson-eva",
        "point": "Olsson favors the bounded, experimentally demonstrated instrument advance of aberration correction and identifies WMAP's large-team attribution and its place within the broader cosmology program as difficult to delimit.",
        "response": "Those are serious concerns, especially the need to establish the proposed trio's roles rather than treat visibility as proof of decisive contribution. WMAP's precision mapping remains distinguishable in principle from COBE's earlier detection and later refinements, but the historical record must support both that distinction and the proposed credit. I retain WMAP provisionally because its quantitative cosmological advance is exceptionally clear."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether Bennett, Spergel, and Page made decisive contributions that fairly represent the larger WMAP collaboration and the wider CMB effort.",
      "How to distinguish WMAP's precision mapping from COBE's earlier detection and subsequent CMB measurements in a historically accurate citation."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
